Agent Command Center (agentcc-gateway) is a high-performance, OpenAI-compatible
LLM gateway written in Go. It sits between your application and LLM providers,
providing a single OpenAI-compatible API for every provider you configure.

Features:
  - One OpenAI-compatible API for OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Bedrock, Cohere,
    Azure, and local self-hosted endpoints
    (vLLM, Ollama, LMStudio, TGI, LocalAI)
  - 15 routing strategies: retries, circuit breakers, failover, hedged/race,
    latency-aware, cost-optimized, model fallback, shadow/mirror, and more
  - Cost control: exact + semantic caching, per-key budgets, quotas, virtual
    keys, rate limits, credits ledger
  - 18 built-in guardrail scanners (PII, injection, jailbreak, secrets,
    hallucination, MCP security, content moderation, and more) plus adapters for
    15 third-party guardrail vendors
  - Observability: Prometheus + OpenTelemetry, per-request metrics
  - Modern protocols: MCP, A2A, Assistants, vector stores, batch, files,
    realtime WebSocket, responses API

Single binary, single YAML config, no proprietary control plane required.
